<title>FRANCE: Rumour Jospin to seek euro delay unfounded - PM offiCE.</title>
<headline>Rumour Jospin to seek euro delay unfounded - PM offiCE.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French Prime Minister's office on Thursday denied a market rumour that Lionel Jospin would ask for a delay of two years for the launch of the euro single currency which is scheduled for January 1, 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;These rumours are totally without foundation,&quot; said an official in Jospin's office.</p>
<p>The franc was not affected by the rumour but some dealers said it was in the market.</p>
</text>
